  "notes": "めくる means to turn, flip, or roll up something flat or layered.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Takes を particle for the object\n\nKANJI NOTE:\nUsually written in hiragana. The kanji {捲|めく}る is rarely used.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ページをめくる: to turn pages\n- カレンダーをめくる: to flip the calendar\n- {布団|ふとん}をめくる: to turn back bedding\n- {袖|そで}をめくる: to roll up sleeves\n- スカートをめくる: to flip up a skirt\n\nASPECT:\nめくっている can describe either the action in progress or a resulting state (e.g., sleeves being rolled up).\n\nRELATED:\n- めくれる (intransitive): to turn over, curl up by itself",
